# Aang, at the Crossroads's ruling (2025-10-02): "its delayed triggered ability won't cause it to transform back into Aang,
# at the Crossroads if it has already transformed into Aang, Destined Savior, perhaps because several creatures left the
# battlefield in one turn" (CR 701.27f: a delayed triggered ability transforms its permanent only if it hasn't transformed
# since that ability was created). On turn 2 Bot2 bolts both of Bot1's Ornithopters, one after the other: Aang triggers
# twice and two delayed abilities wait for the next upkeep, Bot1's on turn 3. Both trigger there; the first transforms Aang,
# the second finds he has transformed since it was created and does nothing, so he is still Aang, Destined Savior.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Black Lotus
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Aang, at the Crossroads
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
